@@ -3,3 +3,14 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` (from `src/index.ts`) implements [RFC 6901](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901).
+It returns the value that a JSON Pointer refers to in a JSON document; the empty pointer `""` refers to the whole document.
+It throws a `JsonPointerError` when the pointer is malformed or does not resolve to a value of the document,
+for example a missing member, an out-of-range array index, or the `-` token.
+
+```ts
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+```
